docs {
  # maptoy API

  Manual smoke requests for a trusted maptoy instance.

  ## Environment

  | Variable | Required for | Value |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | `appUrl` | all requests | Public base URL, including any reverse-proxy prefix; Local defaults to `http://localhost:4004` |
  | `mapSetId` | Map-Set-specific requests | Existing Map Set UUID |
  | `tileZ`, `tileX`, `tileY` | Tile retrieval and seeding | Valid XYZ coordinate for the selected Map Set |
  | `tileRefresh` | Tile retrieval | `auto`, `force`, or `cache-only`; Local defaults to `auto` |
  | `tileFile` | Tile seeding | Absolute path to a PNG, JPEG, or WebP Tile |

  ## Conventions

  - No authorization header is used; maptoy v1 has no application authentication.
  - JSON requests set `Content-Type: application/json`; Tile seeding requires the matching `image/png`, `image/jpeg`, or `image/webp` header.
  - Errors use `error.code` and `error.message`.
  - Requests marked **writes data** create persistent state. Audit requests use POST but are read-only.
}
